page('clients','Client work','''<section class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">02 / The collaborations</span><h1>Client work<span style="color:var(--accent)">.</span></h1><p>From someone else’s idea to a finished piece. A closer look at the brief, the creative process and the work delivered.</p></section><article class="client-case" id="samsonite">'''+samsonite_video()+'''<div class="case-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Samsonite / MethodNMadness</span><h2>Samsonite Recycle X Project</h2><p class="case-intro">During my internship at MethodNMadness, I animated mascots for Samsonite’s Recycle X bag line, bringing their excitement to life through playful, celebratory movement.</p><div class="project-meta"><span class="pill">Mascot animation</span><span class="pill">00:15–00:29</span><span class="pill">2-week project</span></div><dl><dt>The brief</dt><dd>Animate cute mascots to celebrate Samsonite’s new Recycle X bag line.</dd><dt>My contribution</dt><dd>I worked on the shots from 15–29 seconds, animating the mascots in action to convey celebration and excitement.</dd><dt>The delivery</dt><dd>The project ran for two weeks. I refined the animation through minor tweaks with the project manager, and the client was very happy with the delivered results.</dd></dl><details><summary>Credits & project details</summary><p>Client: Samsonite<br>Studio: MethodNMadness<br>My role: mascot animation, as an intern<br>Contribution: shots from 00:15–00:29<br>Project duration: two weeks</p><p>The embedded film shows the full team project; my contribution is limited to the animation work described above.</p></details></div></article><article class="client-case" id="evolved-multimedia"><div class="video-block"><div class="video-frame"><iframe id="evolved-player" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/JxpkbYrDnfQ?rel=0" title="ASCENDA ft. Exo Thrill - HOPE — CG, editing and VFX by Euan Garcia" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><div class="video-caption"><span>Music video · CG, editing & VFX</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JxpkbYrDnfQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch on YouTube ↗</a></div><div class="highlights"><span class="eyebrow">Key highlights</span><div class="highlight-links"><button type="button" data-start="29" data-player="evolved-player" data-video="JxpkbYrDnfQ" data-status="evolved-playback" aria-controls="evolved-player" aria-pressed="false">Light bulb explosion · 0:29</button><button type="button" data-start="53" data-end="59" data-player="evolved-player" data-video="JxpkbYrDnfQ" data-status="evolved-playback" aria-controls="evolved-player" aria-pressed="false">Blender lighting · 0:53–0:59</button><button type="button" data-start="120" data-end="141" data-player="evolved-player" data-video="JxpkbYrDnfQ" data-status="evolved-playback" aria-controls="evolved-player" aria-pressed="false">Blender integration · 2:00–2:21</button><button type="button" data-start="0" data-player="evolved-player" data-video="JxpkbYrDnfQ" data-status="evolved-playback" aria-controls="evolved-player" aria-pressed="false">Full video</button></div><p id="evolved-playback" class="playback-note" role="status" aria-live="polite">Select a highlight to play it in the video above.</p></div></div><div class="case-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Evolved Multimedia / Collaboration</span><h2>ASCENDA ft. Exo Thrill - HOPE</h2><p class="case-intro">Working with Evolved Multimedia again, I captured LIDAR scans and HDRIs to match the scene’s lighting and reflections when integrating CG. My work also covered Blender lighting, video editing and picture lock in Premiere Pro, and VFX in After Effects.</p><div class="project-meta"><span class="pill">LIDAR & HDRI capture</span><span class="pill">Blender</span><span class="pill">Premiere Pro</span><span class="pill">After Effects</span></div><dl><dt>Capturing the scene</dt><dd>I gathered LIDAR scans and HDRIs as references for integrating CG with the filmed environment, matching its lighting and reflections.</dd><dt>CG & lighting</dt><dd>I used Blender to create the floating light and the way it casts and bounces light around the scene. The highlights show the lighting work at 0:53–0:59 and its integration with footage at 2:00–2:21.</dd><dt>Editing & VFX</dt><dd>I edited the video through picture lock in Premiere Pro, then completed VFX in After Effects, including the light bulb explosion at 0:29.</dd></dl><details><summary>Credits & project details</summary><p>Production collaboration: Evolved Multimedia<br>My contribution: LIDAR and HDRI capture, Blender CG and lighting, video editing, picture lock and VFX<br>CG: Blender<br>Editing: Premiere Pro<br>VFX: After Effects</p></details></div></article><div class="end-note"><h2>Beyond the brief.</h2><div><p>Explore my personal films, passion projects and experiments.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/">View My Projects <span>↗</span></a></div></div>''')

